ndText":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"minItems":1,"maxItems":10}],"description":"Find passages instead of paging"},"findMode":{"type":"string","enum":["exact","case-insensitive","fuzzy"]}}}},{"name":"mcp","description":"MCP gateway — URL installation, server status, tool search/describe, auth, and single MCP tool calls. When a user supplies an MCP endpoint URL, install it with the install action. Non-MCP Pi tools should be called directly, not through mcp.\n\nDisabled servers (enable with /mcp-adapter enable <server> and /reload): ghzw\n\nUsage:\n  mcp({ action: \"install\", url: \"https://example.com/mcp\" }) → Install, connect, and authenticate an MCP URL\n  mcp({ })                              → Show server status and tool counts\n  mcp({ server: \"name\" })               → List tools from server\n  mcp({ search: \"query\" })              → Search MCP tools by name/description\n  mcp({ describe: \"tool_name\" })        → Show tool details and parameters\n  mcp({ instructions: \"name\" })         → Show full server usage instructions\n  mcp({ connect: \"server-name\" })       → Connect to a server and refresh metadata\n  mcp({ tool: \"name\", args: { key: \"value\" } })         → Call a tool (object args; JSON string also accepted)\n  mcp({ action: \"ui-messages\" })        → Retrieve accumulated messages from completed UI sessions\n  mcp({ action: \"save-script\", args: { name, description, code, inputSchema } }) → Save a script as a reusable tool (asks you first)\n  mcp({ action: \"auth-start\", server: \"name\" })      → Open OAuth and watch for completion\n  mcp({ action: \"auth-complete\", server: \"name\", args: { redirectUrl: \"...\" } }) → Complete manual OAuth\n\nMode: action > tool (call) > connect > describe > instructions > search > server (list) > nothing (status)\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp(args)` resolves to a string.","parameters":{"type":"object","pro